{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527507849,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMjY5OTgyOTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2577","origin":"github"},"title":"Option to (reversibly) redact run-records","message":"As an alternative to #2576 it would be nice to equip `run` with an option to match anything that would end up in a run-record against an expression, and replace any match with a given string.\n\nThis could be used to redact run-record, making them non-rerunable, but maintain a maximum of information without the infrastructure impact of an encryption solution.\n\nThe re-run aspect could be mitigated via a configurable callable (stored in the datalad config) that can reverse map the replacement string to the original. Such command could be provided in a subdataset to avoid leakage.","files":null}]}